{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgArUCMi85Yd5d2feGdMB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The new UI's root widget wasn't wrapped in `PostHogWidget`, so no replay was recorded for those users. I added the wrapper but haven't run the app, so the fix is unverified.\n\n**Why:** The old shell (`lib/legacy_app.dart`) wraps its `MaterialApp` in `PostHogWidget`. The redesign (`lib/new_app.dart`) returned a bare `MaterialApp.router`. On mobile, Flutter replay is built from screenshots of the widget tree, and `PostHogWidget` takes them. Without it, events like screens, taps and `loan_amount_changed` still arrive, but there are no frames to send. The SDK gives no error or warning. That matches the ticket.\n\n**What I ruled out:**\n- **Project settings:** recording is on, sampling is 100% and minimum duration is 0.\n- **SDK version:** both groups run the same build.\n- **Config:** `sessionReplay = true` is set in `lib/analytics.dart` and shared by both shells.\n- **Observer:** `PosthogObserver` is already on the `GoRouter`.\n\n**Fix:** In `lib/new_app.dart` I wrapped `MaterialApp.router` in `PostHogWidget`, with a comment saying why it must stay. These are the only two root app widgets in `lib/`.\n\n**To verify:** Run the new UI on a device or emulator, visit 3–4 screens, and background the app. The session should then appear in PostHog and play back your screens, not a blank player. The fix only helps once it ships in a release, and sessions from before then can't be recovered.\n\nThe notes are in `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":918,"cache_read_input_tokens":23267,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":918},"output_tokens":545,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_